+// [ios port overlay 0026] The boot config, written on demand.
+//
+// CL_WriteConfig is the ONLY writer of the file the engine execs at boot
+// (COM_CONFIG_CFG in the game directory — see FS_AddConfigFiles), and it runs from
+// CL_Shutdown. A mobile app never reaches CL_Shutdown: the OS kills it. So a phone or
+// headset shell has no way to persist settings into the file that is actually read, and
+// `writeconfig <name>` is not it — that command deliberately writes into `configs/`, which
+// is a *named saved config*, not the boot config. A shell that reached for it wrote a file
+// nothing has ever exec'd.
+//
+// Registered as a command rather than exported as a symbol because the shell already owns a
+// console seam (and only a console seam) for talking to the engine from its lifecycle
+// callbacks. Nothing on desktop calls it, so the reference build is unchanged.
+static void CL_WriteBootConfig_f(void)
+{
+    CL_WriteConfig();
+}
