+
+// [ios port overlay 0026] Re-derive ONLY the HUD scale after r_config changed, with none of
+// SCR_ModeChanged's other work. A VR world frame lays its HUD out for a widescreen sub-rect
+// of a nearly-square eye target, so r_config changes twice per rendered frame — and at 90 Hz
+// neither Con_CheckResize's full console reflow nor UI_ModeChanged's menu rebuild can be paid
+// for twice a frame. Neither is needed there: a VR frame that has a menu or the console up is
+// routed to a different surface entirely, so the only 2D inside the bracket is the HUD, whose
+// layout depends on r_config and this scale and nothing else. Unused off that path — no
+// caller on desktop, so the reference build's behaviour is byte-identical.
+void SCR_HudScaleChanged(void)
+{
+    if (scr.initialized)
+        scr.hud_scale = R_ClampScale(scr_scale);
 }
 
